<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gilukhipa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 14th century BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gilukhipa was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a> princess, daughter of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shuttarna-ii">Shuttarna II</a>, who was sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> to marry <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">Pharaoh</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/amenhotep-iii">Amenhotep III</a> in his tenth regnal year, around 1380 BCE. A commemorative scarab records her arrival with 317 women of her household. The marriage sealed the alliance between Egypt and Mitanni, and her niece <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tadukhipa">Tadukhipa</a> later followed her to the Egyptian court.</p></div>
